只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Archived standalone Browser and historical releases. Active Desktop + Browser project: ManoloRemiddi/augmentor-agent.","id":"gh:1344900437","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"augmentor-dsh-extension-plugin","slug":"ManoloRemiddi/augmentor-dsh-extension-plugin","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","manolo-dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Archived standalone Browser and historical releases. Active Desktop + Browser project: ManoloRemiddi"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ne Browser and historical releases. Active Desktop + Browser project: ManoloRemiddi/augmentor-agent."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"## Archived workspace — September 23, 2026"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"This is the archived standalone Browser repository. The only active Augmentor Desktop + Browser repo"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"sitory is\nManoloRemiddi/augmentor-agent, default branch **main**.\nCurrent source, issues, pull reque"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"sts and future releases belong there.\nExisting history, licenses and release downloads are retained "},{"id":"p3s4","text":"here.\nDo not repoint this checkout at the active public origin or merge its history.\nPreserve local "},{"id":"p3s5","text":"changes and port only selected, privacy-reviewed changes onto a\nfresh canonical branch. Older develo"},{"id":"p3s6","text":"pment directions below are historical.\nSee repository map and preserved work."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"# Augmentor, powered by DSH"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**Augmentor** turns any DeepSeek Harness (DSH) web session into a browser\noperator: a Chrome side pa"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"nel chats with your DSH app, and the agent drives\nyour *real* browser — live accessibility snapshot,"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" click, type, tab switching —\nwith the user watching every action pulse on the actual page. Chats ar"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"e real\nDSH sessions in a dedicated directory, and **Save** attaches the current chat\nto a DSH worksp"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"al\nDSH sessions in a dedicated directory, and **Save** attaches the current chat\nto a DSH workspace."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"No sidecar runtime, no second DSH process: the extension talks to the **running**\nDSH app over its s"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"tock `/api` surface (the pipe is the browser's loopback\nstand-in client, because the extension's Ori"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"gin is refused by the DSH trust\nfence — by design)."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Components"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| path | what it is |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| `extension/` | MV3 Chrome extension: side panel chat, service worker (native port + browser execut"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"or), page veil, work-tab overlays, theme tokens |\n| `pipe.mjs` | native messaging host: loopback bri"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"dge to the DSH app's `/api` surface, downlinks, plugin channel |\n| `plugin/` | the `dsh-augmentor` D"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"SH plugin (npm package + git bundle): `/api/augmentor` handshake, pipe WS channel, `browser_*` tools"},{"id":"p10s5","text":", chat lifecycle |\n| `wire.mjs` | the shared wire primitives (frame codec + pending table) used by a"},{"id":"p10s6","text":"ll three runtimes — one implementation, three consumers |\n| `install-native-host.sh` | installs the "},{"id":"p10s7","text":"Chromium native-messaging-host manifest + the per-machine channel token |\n| `test/` | e2e suites (m3"},{"id":"p10s8","text":", sw, panel, chrome, m2, tools) + `install-proof.mjs` (deterministic fresh-user install proof) + `pl"},{"id":"p10s9","text":"ugin/tests/boot/` |\n| `PROPOSAL-plugin-architecture.md` | the architecture record: milestones M1–M4,"},{"id":"p10s10","text":" audit findings S/D/F, decisions |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## DSH compatibility"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Augmentor 0.1.32 targets **DSH 0.1.5-rc.1** and its authenticated Typert API.\nUpgrade the plugin, na"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"tive host and extension together. Augmentor 0.1.31\nand earlier do not work with this DSH release: th"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"eir SDK dependency,\nHTTP method names, authentication and event streams predate the new API."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"To update an existing installation after installing this release:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Restart DSH and reload Augmentor at `chrome://extensions`. For the npm\nplugin path, use `dsh plugin "},{"id":"p15s2","text":"--profile web add dsh-augmentor@0.1.32` from npm. The installer reconciles dependencies, installs\nth"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"e Augmentor preset when missing, and backs up a legacy preset before\nrenaming its persona `text` set"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"ting to `prefix`. A custom `DSH_HOME` must\nbe the same for DSH, the installer and the browser/native"},{"id":"p15s5","text":"o `prefix`. A custom `DSH_HOME` must\nbe the same for DSH, the installer and the browser/native host."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"The bridge exchanges DSH's launch token through a local endpoint protected\nby Augmentor's existing a"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"ction-channel secret. Its session cookie remains\ninside the native host. No extension cookie permiss"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"ion or disabled DSH\nauthentication is required."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Tested on **Linux with Chromium**, Node.js 22.19+ or 24+, and DSH 0.1.5-rc.1."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"1. Install/update DSH: `npm install -g @deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.5-rc.1`.\n2. Download Augmentor 0.1.32 ZI"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"P and extract the entire\n`augmentor-0.1.32` folder to a permanent location. It includes the plugin,\n"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"extension, native host and preset. Keep all the files together.\nSource alternative: `git clone --bra"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"nch v0.1.32 https://github.com/ManoloRemiddi/augmentor-dsh-extension-plugin.git`.\n3. Open `chrome://"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"extensions`, enable **Developer mode**, choose **Load unpacked**,\nselect `extension/` in the extract"},{"id":"p19s6","text":"ed folder and copy the extension ID.\n4. From the extracted folder, run `sh install-native-host.sh EX"},{"id":"p19s7","text":"TENSION_ID \"$HOME/.config/chromium\"`\nwith that ID. The second argument is the browser user-data root"},{"id":"p19s8","text":", not `Default`.\nOther Linux defaults: Chrome `~/.config/google-chrome`, Edge `~/.config/microsoft-e"},{"id":"p19s9","text":"dge`,\nBrave `~/.config/BraveSoftware/Brave-Browser`. Other platforms are not verified;\nthese shell c"},{"id":"p19s10","text":"ommands are not a Windows installer.\n5. In the same folder, run `dsh plugin --profile web add \"$PWD/"},{"id":"p19s11","text":"plugin\"`.\nAlternatively install `dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-augmentor@0.1.32`.\nChoose one meth"},{"id":"p19s12","text":"od and use your app's actual profile if different from `web`.\nPinning the npm version avoids an olde"},{"id":"p19s13","text":"r release being selected by release-age filtering.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Security posture"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"- **The DSH trust fence is why the pipe exists — it is not bypassed.** The\nDSH app's `/api` refuses "},{"id":"p21s2","text":"requests from foreign browser origins (the\nextension's `chrome-extension://` origin included, by des"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"ign). `pipe.mjs`\nis a loopback stand-in client: it runs locally as the user and talks to\nthe app ove"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"r `127.0.0.1`, which is exactly what the fence permits.\n- **No new remote surface.** Every hop is lo"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"opback (extension ↔ pipe via\nnative messaging, pipe ↔ app via `127.0.0.1`); nothing this stack adds "},{"id":"p21s6","text":"is\nreachable from other hosts. The trust boundary is the local OS user:\nanything that can already re"},{"id":"p21s7","text":"ad your home directory is not blocked by this\nstack (and could already do the same things directly a"},{"id":"p21s8","text":"gainst the app).\n- **The action channel is secret-gated.** The `browser_*` commands flow over\na WS c"},{"id":"p21s9","text":"hannel the plugin authenticates with a per-machine token\n(`$DSH_HOME/augmentor-ws-token`, 0600, crea"},{"id":"p21s10","text":"ted by the installer or first\nboot; a configured `actionToken` wins). The pipe presents it in the WS"},{"id":"p21s11","text":"\nhandshake header and the plugin compares it in constant time; a local\nprocess without that file can"},{"id":"p21s12","text":"not drive your browser.\n- **The in-panel \"Trust-fence probe\"** (≣ Sessions → *Probe*) is a diagnosti"},{"id":"p21s13","text":"c\nthat shows the fence working as designed (extension-origin requests\nrefused, loopback requests acc"},{"id":"p21s14","text":"epted). It probes; it does not bypass."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
